  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The molar heat capacity for an ideal gas at constant pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>785</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The change in internal energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> upon heating it from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The number of moles of the gas at constant volume is____</p><p>(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Molar specific heat capacity at constant pressure is defined as the amount of heat energy required to raise the temperature of one mole of a substance through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> at constant pressure. It is denoted by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub></math>.</p><p>Molar specific heat capacity at constant volume&nbsp;is defined as the amount of heat energy required to raise the temperature of one mole of a substance through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> at constant volume. It is denoted by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>785</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>471</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Jk</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>ml</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>nC</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mi>&#916;T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5000</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>471</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>471</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
